# Product language

In **code comments**, **CLI/help**, **README**, **Astro docs** (`docs/content/`), **`.ai/docs/`**, and other product/dev-facing text: product vocabulary only. Planning jargon belongs only in `.ai/specs/`.

**Never write:** `Tryb A/B`, `tor A/B`, `Faza 0…13` / `Faza W` / `DoD` as status, `option C`, “no Mitosis”, “formerly ww-workflow”, roadmap voice (“leftovers”, “slice”, “deferred”, “tracked separately”), issue numbers as section titles unless the user asked for a changelog.

**Prefer:** canonical Nuxt (`web/`, `admin/`); product convert / generated shells (`web-next/`, …); emit / convert / import / CI; IR-first / custom IR. Ordinary Polish (*tryb pracy*, *tryb ciemny*) is fine — do not invent **Tryb A/B**.

Chat may discuss plans; do not paste that jargon into repo files outside `.ai/specs/`.
